Q: How to anonymize PII before sending data to GPT APIs? A: <p>If have done something similar in Microsoft Foundry: you can use <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/ai-services/language-service/personally-identifiable-information/how-to/redact-text-pii" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Azure Language - Text PII Redaction</a>.</p>
<p>In Foundry, enable the LLM you are going to use as well as Azure Language. I would also enable PII blocking in a custom guardrail in Foundry to make sure no PII get's sent to the llm. The first step would be send the user input text to <code>Azure Language - Text PII Redaction</code>. You will get a json back so you can send the <code>redactedText</code> to the llm, take the llm response and map the <code>mask</code> back to the <code>text</code> and you should be good to go.</p>
<p>Here is the json response for your sample input text.</p>
<pre><code>{
  &quot;documents&quot;: [
    {
      &quot;redactedText&quot;: &quot;[PERSON-1] from [ORGANIZATION-2] called me at [PHONENUMBER-3]&quot;,
      &quot;id&quot;: &quot;1&quot;,
      &quot;entities&quot;: [
        {
          &quot;text&quot;: &quot;John Smith&quot;,
          &quot;category&quot;: &quot;Person&quot;,
          &quot;type&quot;: &quot;Person&quot;,
          &quot;offset&quot;: 0,
          &quot;length&quot;: 10,
          &quot;mask&quot;: &quot;[PERSON-1]&quot;,
          &quot;maskOffset&quot;: 0,
          &quot;maskLength&quot;: 10,
          &quot;confidenceScore&quot;: 1,
          &quot;tags&quot;: [
            {
              &quot;name&quot;: &quot;Person&quot;,
              &quot;confidenceScore&quot;: 1
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          &quot;text&quot;: &quot;ACME Corp&quot;,
          &quot;category&quot;: &quot;Organization&quot;,
          &quot;type&quot;: &quot;Organization&quot;,
          &quot;offset&quot;: 16,
